  "problem": "The random variable $X$ has the following probability distribution.\n\n| $x$ | $-3$ | $-1$ | $1$ | $3$ | $9$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $0.35$ | $0.15$ | $0.15$ | $0.1$ | $0.25$ |\n\nCalculate $P({X}^{2}=9).$",
  "worked_solution": "Let's first add an ${X}^{2}$ row to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $-3$ | $-1$ | $1$ | $3$ | $9$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${x}^{2}$ | $9$ | $1$ | $1$ | $9$ | $81$ |\n| $f(x)$ | $0.35$ | $0.15$ | $0.15$ | $0.1$ | $0.25$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFrom the second and third rows of our table, we can immediately conclude that \n\n$$\nP({X}^{2}=9)=0.35+0.1=0.45.\n$$",
